## TWO LIVE DEFECTS FOUND DURING READBACK (both fixed + redeployed + re-proven)

1. **BC-5 was non-functional — all four forms detailTypes UNREGISTERED.**
   `publish()` throws on unregistered detailType (`audit-trail-registry.ts` contract);
   `FormRecord.Submitted/Reopened/Approved` and `Security.SodViolationBlocked` were
   never added by spec-41 Tasks 5/6. Every audit publish from forms.ts threw —
   invisible to hermetic tests (publishAuditEvent mocked), and masked live by defect 2.
   FIX: 4 registry entries + contracts/events.md rows (parity test green).
2. **Rollback-after-commit masked the true error.** submit's catch ran a raw
   `txn.rollback()` after a post-commit failure → `TransactionNotFoundException`
   replaced the real error (the unregistered-detailType throw). The Task-6 approve
   guard existed but not elsewhere. FIX: all 12 rollback sites in forms.ts are now
   `try { rollback } catch { /* never mask the original error */ }` (mock-agnostic form).
   NOTE: the failed submit was still ATOMIC — record complete + m2 rows all committed;
   only the error report was wrong.

